+| A task has fewer planned slots than k | mark ineligible; no fixed-suite macro under this policy | inventing zero/perfect score or silently excluding task |
+| Claim about future IID trials | state fixed design, stable per-task probability and IID assumptions | treating exact finite-panel proportions as sampling CIs |
+
+Checklist: name the event and task population; preserve planned slot identities;
+separate valid failures from unresolved outcomes; report per-task n,c,u and
+macro weighting; distinguish identification bounds from uncertainty due to
+sampling; state what the source code says separately from what was executed.
+Manual worked examples validate these interpretations only. No new gate/probe
